Flexbox centers the panel on both axes. The parent needs a height, such as min-height: 100vh, for vertical centering to be visible.

```
.game-screen {
  min-height: 100vh;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
}
```

Grid creates the columns and gap adds spacing. The media query changes the layout to one column on narrower screens.

```
.game-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 12px;
}

@media (max-width: 650px) {
  .game-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
```

The :hover rule applies while a pointer is over the button. Keep a visible keyboard focus style as well.

```
.play-button {
  background: #2563eb;
  color: white;
  transition: background-color 150ms ease;
}

.play-button:hover {
  background: #1d4ed8;
}
```

The click listener runs after the user presses the button. Make sure both elements exist before this script runs, for example by using defer on the script tag.

```
const button = document.querySelector('#showPanel');
const panel = document.querySelector('#panel');

button.addEventListener('click', () => {
  panel.hidden = false;
});
```

The variable stores the count. Each click increases it and updates the page text.

```
let clicks = 0;
