ctx.fillRect(player.x, player.y, player.width, player.height);
```

The loop updates the game, draws a frame, and requests another frame. Define update and draw before this loop runs.

```
function gameLoop(time) {
  update(time);
  draw();
  requestAnimationFrame(gameLoop);
}

requestAnimationFrame(gameLoop);
```

The keys object records pressed state. The keyup listener resets it so movement stops when the key is released.

```
const keys = {};

window.addEventListener('keydown', event => {
  if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') keys.right = true;
});

window.addEventListener('keyup', event => {
  if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') keys.right = false;
});
```

dt is elapsed time in seconds. Multiplying speed by dt makes movement depend on time rather than frame count.

```
const player = { x: 0, speed: 180 };

function update(dt) {
  player.x += player.speed * dt;
}
```

The function checks for overlap on both the horizontal and vertical axes. It works for axis-aligned rectangles.

```
function overlaps(a, b) {
  return a.x < b.x + b.width &&
         a.x + a.width > b.x &&
         a.y < b.y + b.height &&
         a.y + a.height > b.y;
}
```

Pointer Events work with touch, mouse, and pen. Resetting the state on pointerup and pointercancel helps prevent a control from staying pressed.

```
const button = document.querySelector('#jumpButton');

button.addEventListener('pointerdown', () => {
  player.jumpRequested = true;
});

button.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {
  player.jumpRequested = false;
});

button.addEventListener('pointercancel', () => {
  player.jumpRequested = false;
});
```

