Why does this element not get selected?

HTML: <p id="score">0</p>
JS: const score = document.getElementById('#score');

Why does this check behave incorrectly?

let health = 3;
if (health = 0) {
  console.log('game over');
}

A single = assigns a value. Three equals signs compare values without type conversion.

Use strict equality to compare instead of assignment:
```
if (health === 0) {
  console.log('game over');
}
```

