Why is align-items not centering my panel?

.parent {
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
}

align-items and justify-content control flex alignment only when the parent uses display: flex (or the relevant grid layout).

Turn the parent into a flex container:
```
.parent {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
}
```

Why are my grid columns not appearing?

.cards {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
}

grid-template-columns defines tracks, but the element needs display: grid to use CSS Grid.

Set display: grid on the container:
```
.cards {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 12px;
}
```

A fixed CSS width can overflow on a narrow screen. For a game canvas, also manage its internal width and height in JavaScript so drawing coordinates remain correct.

Make the displayed canvas responsive while setting its drawing resolution separately:
```
canvas {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 900px;
  height: auto;
}
```

